# botskills rollback ledger

One entry per production state we may need to return to. Newest at the bottom.
To roll back, pick the entry and follow docs/ROLLBACK.md with its values:
Vercel alias rollback first (seconds, no rebuild), then git revert on main.

Entry format:
  date (UTC)   what this state is
  git ref      commit and, where one exists, the backup branch pointing at it
  vercel       the production deployment URL that served this exact state
  verify       what to curl to prove the rollback took

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2026-09-03 20:35 UTC   Before the first code refactor (helpers, tests, hubs).
  git ref   8bf3f14   branch backup/pre-refactor-2026-09-03 (on origin)
  vercel    https://botskills-c961mtbz4-luckydutta96s-projects.vercel.app
  verify    curl -s https://botskills.sh/sponsor | sed 's/<!-- -->//g' | grep -o 'There are [0-9]* bot listings'
            prints "37" (the old literal) in this state; the live count after.

2026-09-04 18:10 UTC   After the refactor, growth items 1/2/4/5/8, and the
                       first platform-fact corrections (Android page rewrite).
  git ref   abe7930
  vercel    https://botskills-iu8fbda0d-luckydutta96s-projects.vercel.app
  verify    curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' https://botskills.sh/integrations/gmail   -> 200

2026-09-06 15:20 UTC   Before the second refactor and the 150-article platform
                       sweep. Production at this moment was botskills-4qnvdgq9k.
  git ref   abe7930   branch backup/pre-refactor-2026-09-06 (on origin)
  vercel    https://botskills-4qnvdgq9k-luckydutta96s-projects.vercel.app
            (created 2026-09-04 14:01 UTC; verified to serve the growth work at
            abe7930, including /integrations, and none of the 2026-09-05 WIP)
  verify    curl -s https://botskills.sh/blog/grok-bot-troubleshooting | grep -o 'No Linux desktop, Android, or iPad app'
            matches in this state (the old table row); no match after the sweep.
